inference_trace:
The minimum number of operations equals the sum of the prime factors of `n` (counted with multiplicity). Getting from 1 to `n` means multiplying the count by each prime factor `p` in turn. Each multiplication by `p` costs one Copy All plus `p-1` Pastes, which is `p` operations.

The code divides out each factor `d` starting from 2 and adds `d` to the answer every time it divides evenly. For `n = 1` no factors exist, so it returns 0.

```java
class Solution {
    public int minSteps(int n) {
        int res = 0;
        for (int d = 2; d <= n; d++) {
            while (n % d == 0) {
                res += d;
                n /= d;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

