inference_trace:
The approach is to strip the parentheses, split the digit string into a left part and a right part at every possible position, and combine every valid representation of each part.

To generate the valid numbers for a digit string `t` of length n:
- Try each split point i from 1 to n. The integer part is `t[0..i)` and the fractional part is `t[i..n)`.
- The integer part is invalid if it has a leading zero and length greater than 1.
- The fractional part is invalid if it is non-empty and ends with `0`.
- If i == n there is no fractional part, so the number is just the integer part.

Checks against the examples:
- "0" gives i=1 and the integer "0", which is valid.
- "00" gives i=1 with integer "0" and fraction "0", which ends in 0 and is invalid. i=2 gives integer "00", which has a leading zero and is invalid. So there are no results, as expected.
- "01" gives i=1 with integer "0" and fraction "1", so "0.1". i=2 gives "01", which is invalid. The only result is "0.1", as expected.

The input has the form "(123)", possibly with a trailing space as in the examples. The constraints say `s[last] == ')'`, so I use `s.substring(1, s.length() - 1)`. The output format is "(a, b)".

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public List<String> ambiguousCoordinates(String s) {
        String d = s.substring(1, s.length() - 1);
        List<String> res = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 1; i < d.length(); i++) {
            List<String> l = gen(d.substring(0, i));
            if (l.isEmpty()) continue;
            List<String> r = gen(d.substring(i));
            for (String a : l) {
                for (String b : r) {
                    res.add("(" + a + ", " + b + ")");
                }
            }
        }
        return res;
    }

    private List<String> gen(String t) {
        List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();
        int n = t.length();
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            String ip = t.substring(0, i);
            String fp = t.substring(i);
            if (ip.length() > 1 && ip.charAt(0) == '0') continue;
            if (!fp.isEmpty() && fp.charAt(fp.length() - 1) == '0') continue;
            out.add(fp.isEmpty() ? ip : ip + "." + fp);
        }
        return out;
    }
}
```

