inference_trace:
Track the sum, minimum and maximum in one pass, then subtract the minimum and maximum from the sum and divide by `n - 2`. The sum is kept in a `long` so it cannot overflow, although with at most 100 salaries of at most 10^6 it stays small anyway.

```java
class Solution {
    public double average(int[] salary) {
        long sum = 0;
        int min = Integer.MAX_VALUE, max = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        for (int s : salary) {
            sum += s;
            min = Math.min(min, s);
            max = Math.max(max, s);
        }
        return (double) (sum - min - max) / (salary.length - 2);
    }
}
```

