inference_trace:
Count how often each character appears, then check that every character that appears has the same count.

Note that the examples show a trailing space in the strings (e.g. "abacbc "). The constraints say the input is lowercase letters only, so I won't special-case it. To be safe, I count over all 128 ASCII values instead of just 26 letters. If a trailing space did appear, it would count as a character, which is the literal reading of the problem.

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean areOccurrencesEqual(String s) {
        int[] cnt = new int[128];
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            cnt[s.charAt(i) & 127]++;
        }
        int f = 0;
        for (int c : cnt) {
            if (c == 0) continue;
            if (f == 0) f = c;
            else if (f != c) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

