inference_trace:
The maximum OR is the OR of all elements, since OR never loses bits as more elements are added. With at most 16 elements, I can count the subsets that reach this maximum by recursing over include/exclude choices for each element.

Every element is at least 1, so any non-empty subset is non-zero. The empty subset has OR 0, which is less than the maximum, so it is never counted.

```java
class Solution {
    int target;
    int count;

    public int countMaxOrSubsets(int[] nums) {
        target = 0;
        for (int x : nums) target |= x;
        count = 0;
        dfs(nums, 0, 0);
        return count;
    }

    private void dfs(int[] nums, int i, int cur) {
        if (i == nums.length) {
            if (cur == target) count++;
            return;
        }
        dfs(nums, i + 1, cur | nums[i]);
        dfs(nums, i + 1, cur);
    }
}
```

