Approach: build prefix sums for rows, columns, and both diagonals. Then try each side length k from min(m,n) down to 2. For each top-left corner, check that all row sums, column sums, and both diagonal sums equal the first row's sum, and return the first k that works. If none works, return 1.

Prefix arrays (sizes (m+1) x (n+1) are enough, with some care):
- `row[i][j+1] = row[i][j] + grid[i][j]`, the prefix sum along row i.
- `col[i+1][j] = col[i][j] + grid[i][j]`, the prefix sum along column j.
- `d1[i+1][j+1] = d1[i][j] + grid[i][j]`, the main-diagonal prefix.
- `d2[i+1][j] = d2[i][j+1] + grid[i][j]`, the anti-diagonal prefix. This needs width n+1, and index j+1 ≤ n is fine.

For a square with top-left (i,j) and size k:
- Target sum: `t = row[i][j+k] - row[i][j]`.
- Main diagonal: `d1[i+k][j+k] - d1[i][j]`.
- Anti-diagonal: it runs from (i, j+k-1) down to (i+k-1, j). Using `d2[r+1][c] = d2[r][c+1] + g[r][c]`, we get `d2[i+k][j] - d2[i][j+k]`. Check: d2[i+k][j] accumulates the cells (i+k-1, j), (i+k-2, j+1), ..., (i, j+k-1), and then continues to d2[i][j+k], which is subtracted. This is correct.
- Rows: check each r in i..i+k-1.
- Columns: check each c in j..j+k-1 with `col[i+k][c] - col[i][c]`.

Complexity is about 50 · 2500 · 100 operations, which is fine.

```java
class Solution {
    public int largestMagicSquare(int[][] grid) {
        int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
        int[][] row = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        int[][] col = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        int[][] d1 = new int[m + 1][n + 1];
        int[][] d2 = new int[m + 1][n + 2];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                int g = grid[i][j];
                row[i][j + 1] = row[i][j] + g;
                col[i + 1][j] = col[i][j] + g;
                d1[i + 1][j + 1] = d1[i][j] + g;
                d2[i + 1][j] = d2[i][j + 1] + g;
            }
        }
        for (int k = Math.min(m, n); k >= 2; k--) {
            for (int i = 0; i + k <= m; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j + k <= n; j++) {
                    int t = row[i][j + k] - row[i][j];
                    if (d1[i + k][j + k] - d1[i][j] != t) continue;
                    if (d2[i + k][j] - d2[i][j + k] != t) continue;
                    boolean ok = true;
                    for (int r = i; r < i + k && ok; r++) {
                        if (row[r][j + k] - row[r][j] != t) ok = false;
                    }
                    for (int c = j; c < j + k && ok; c++) {
                        if (col[i + k][c] - col[i][c] != t) ok = false;
                    }
                    if (ok) return k;
                }
            }
        }
        return 1;
    }
}
```

