For each mask with an even popcount, take the lowest unset bit `i` and pair it with every other unset bit `j`. This is valid because `i` must be paired with something, so fixing it avoids counting the same pairing in different orders. Then:

`dp[mask | (1<<i) | (1<<j)] = max(..., dp[mask] + (ops + 1) * gcd[i][j])`

The pairwise gcds are precomputed. There are 2^14 masks with at most 14 transitions each, which is small.

The lowest-unset-bit rule is safe because the operation index depends only on how many pairs have been removed, not on which ones. Every perfect matching is therefore reachable, in every order of its pairs, by choosing which pair gets which index. Fixing the lowest unset element enumerates the pairs in an order determined by their lowest elements, which is just one ordering of the pairs. That is not enough, since the scores depend on the order.

So the lowest-bit restriction is wrong here, and the transition must try all pairs `(i, j)` of unset bits. That is at most C(14,2) = 91 pairs per mask, giving about 16384 × 91 ≈ 1.5M operations, which is fine.

Unreachable masks hold `-1` and are skipped. Masks with odd popcount are skipped too.

```java
class Solution {
    public int maxScore(int[] nums) {
        int m = nums.length;
        int[][] g = new int[m][m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++)
                g[i][j] = gcd(nums[i], nums[j]);
        int full = 1 << m;
        int[] dp = new int[full];
        java.util.Arrays.fill(dp, -1);
        dp[0] = 0;
        int best = 0;
        for (int mask = 0; mask < full; mask++) {
            if (dp[mask] < 0) continue;
            int pc = Integer.bitCount(mask);
            if ((pc & 1) == 1) continue;
            int op = pc / 2 + 1;
            if (pc == m) {
                best = Math.max(best, dp[mask]);
                continue;
            }
            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << i)) != 0) continue;
                for (int j = i + 1; j < m; j++) {
                    if ((mask & (1 << j)) != 0) continue;
                    int nm = mask | (1 << i) | (1 << j);
                    int v = dp[mask] + op * g[i][j];
                    if (v > dp[nm]) dp[nm] = v;
                }
            }
        }
        return best;
    }

    private int gcd(int a, int b) {
        return b == 0 ? a : gcd(b, a % b);
    }
}
```

