inference_trace:
Binary search on the running time T. A time T is feasible if the sum of min(b, T) over all batteries is at least n*T. A battery can contribute at most T minutes, since it can only run one computer at a time. Given that, the contributions can be scheduled across the n computers.

The upper bound is sum/n, which is at most 1e14 (1e5 batteries × 1e9 each, divided by n ≥ 1). So the search range is lo = 1 up to hi = sum/n.

Overflow check: n*T ≤ sum ≤ 1e14, which fits in a long. The sum of min(b, T) is also at most 1e14.

```java
class Solution {
    public long maxRunTime(int n, int[] batteries) {
        long sum = 0;
        for (int b : batteries) sum += b;
        long lo = 0, hi = sum / n;
        while (lo < hi) {
            long mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2;
            long tot = 0;
            for (int b : batteries) tot += Math.min((long) b, mid);
            if (tot >= mid * n) lo = mid;
            else hi = mid - 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }
}
```

