This is a row-by-row bitmask DP. Each row's state is a bitmask of seated students.

A mask is valid for a row if:
- it only uses good seats, i.e. `mask & ~avail == 0`;
- it has no two adjacent students, i.e. `mask & (mask >> 1) == 0`.

Two consecutive rows, with masks `prev` and `cur`, are compatible if `cur & (prev << 1) == 0` and `cur & (prev >> 1) == 0`. This covers the upper-left and upper-right cases, and directly in front or behind is allowed.

The recurrence is `dp[i][cur] = max over compatible prev of dp[i-1][prev] + popcount(cur)`. Invalid states are marked with -1. For the first row, `prev` is 0 with value 0, so I start with `dp[0] = 0` and all other states -1 before row 0.

The input may contain characters like `'.'` or `'#'`. The examples show strings with trailing spaces, but the actual input is a `char[][]`, so I treat `'.'` as good and everything else as broken.

```java
class Solution {
    public int maxStudents(char[][] seats) {
        int m = seats.length, n = seats[0].length;
        int full = 1 << n;
        int[] dp = new int[full];
        java.util.Arrays.fill(dp, -1);
        dp[0] = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            int avail = 0;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (seats[i][j] == '.') avail |= 1 << j;
            }
            int[] nd = new int[full];
            java.util.Arrays.fill(nd, -1);
            for (int cur = 0; cur < full; cur++) {
                if ((cur & ~avail) != 0) continue;
                if ((cur & (cur >> 1)) != 0) continue;
                int cnt = Integer.bitCount(cur);
                for (int prev = 0; prev < full; prev++) {
                    if (dp[prev] < 0) continue;
                    if ((cur & (prev << 1)) != 0) continue;
                    if ((cur & (prev >> 1)) != 0) continue;
                    nd[cur] = Math.max(nd[cur], dp[prev] + cnt);
                }
            }
            dp = nd;
        }
        int best = 0;
        for (int v : dp) best = Math.max(best, v);
        return best;
    }
}
```

