inference_trace:
Sort the array and take elements from the largest down, stopping as soon as the taken sum is strictly greater than the remaining sum. Taking the largest elements first gives the minimum size and, among those, the maximum total sum. The result comes out in non-increasing order.

Steps:
1. Compute the total sum.
2. Sort `nums` ascending.
3. Iterate from the end, adding each element to the result and to a running sum.
4. Stop when the running sum exceeds `total - running`.

The code uses `java.util.*`, so I include the import above the class; the class and method signature are unchanged.

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public List<Integer> minSubsequence(int[] nums) {
        int total = 0;
        for (int x : nums) total += x;
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int cur = 0;
        for (int i = nums.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            cur += nums[i];
            res.add(nums[i]);
            if (cur > total - cur) break;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

