inference_trace:
Convert each date to a day count since a fixed reference year (1971), then return the absolute difference.

For a date, the day count is the total days in all full years before its year, plus the days in all full months before its month, plus the day of the month. A leap year is divisible by 4 and not by 100, or divisible by 400. In the range 1971–2100 this matters for 2000 (leap) and 2100 (not leap), and the general rule handles both.

```java
class Solution {
    private boolean leap(int y) {
        return (y % 4 == 0 && y % 100 != 0) || y % 400 == 0;
    }

    private int toDays(String s) {
        int y = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(0, 4));
        int m = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(5, 7));
        int d = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(8, 10));
        int[] md = {31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31};
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 1971; i < y; i++) {
            total += leap(i) ? 366 : 365;
        }
        for (int i = 1; i < m; i++) {
            total += md[i - 1];
            if (i == 2 && leap(y)) total++;
        }
        return total + d;
    }

    public int daysBetweenDates(String date1, String date2) {
        return Math.abs(toDays(date1) - toDays(date2));
    }
}
```

