4. For each reachable mask and each element `i` not in the mask, let `v = dp[mask] + nums[i]`. If `v <= target`, set `dp[mask | 1<<i] = v % target`.
5. Each element is only added when it fits in the current partial subset, so a full subset resets to 0 exactly when it reaches `target`. The answer is `dp[full] == 0`.

