This is the classic problem of choosing n non-adjacent slices from a circular array of 3n slices, maximizing their sum.

Handle the circle by solving two linear cases and taking the larger result:
1. Use slices[0..m-2], which excludes the last slice.
2. Use slices[1..m-1], which excludes the first slice.

For each linear array, let dp[i][j] be the best sum using the first i elements with j chosen and no two adjacent. The recurrence is dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i-2][j-1] + a[i-1]).

Implementation details:
- Use dp of size (len+1) x (n+1).
- dp[0][*] = 0 for j = 0. For j > 0 with i = 0, the state is invalid, so use a very negative value.
- For i = 1, dp[i-2] would be out of range, so treat the previous value as 0 when j = 1 and invalid otherwise. This is simplest by indexing with an offset: allocate dp[len+2][n+1], where row index i+1 represents the first i elements. Row 0 and row 1 both mean "0 elements", with dp = 0 for j = 0 and -inf otherwise.
- With the offset, for i from 1 to len: dp[i+1][j] = max(dp[i][j], dp[i-1][j-1] + a[i-1]), where dp[i] means the first i-1 elements. Here dp[i-1] is the state with the first i-2 elements, which is correct because we skip element i-2.

Check on a small case: len = 1, j = 1. dp[2][1] = max(dp[1][1] = -inf, dp[0][0] + a[0] = a[0]) = a[0]. Correct.

The answer for each case is dp[len+1][n]. The size is at most 500 x 167, which is tiny.

Edge case: slices.length = 1 gives n = 1 and m = 1, so both linear arrays are empty and the answer should be slices[0]. Handle this separately. For m = 3 (n = 1), the arrays have length 2 and we pick one element, which works.

```java
class Solution {
    public int maxSizeSlices(int[] slices) {
        int m = slices.length;
        int n = m / 3;
        if (m == 1) return slices[0];
        int a = solve(slices, 0, m - 2, n);
        int b = solve(slices, 1, m - 1, n);
        return Math.max(a, b);
    }

    private int solve(int[] s, int lo, int hi, int n) {
        int len = hi - lo + 1;
        int NEG = -1000000000;
        int[][] dp = new int[len + 2][n + 1];
        for (int i = 0; i < len + 2; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) dp[i][j] = NEG;
            dp[i][0] = 0;
        }
        for (int i = 1; i <= len; i++) {
            int v = s[lo + i - 1];
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                int best = dp[i][j];
                int prev = dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                if (prev > NEG / 2) best = Math.max(best, prev + v);
                dp[i + 1][j] = best;
            }
        }
        return dp[len + 1][n];
    }
}
```

