The two rectangles overlap with positive area exactly when their projections overlap with positive length on both axes.

- On the x-axis, the overlap length is `min(rec1[2], rec2[2]) - max(rec1[0], rec2[0])`, which must be greater than 0.
- On the y-axis, the overlap length is `min(rec1[3], rec2[3]) - max(rec1[1], rec2[1])`, which must be greater than 0.

Rectangles that only touch along an edge or at a corner give an overlap length of 0 on at least one axis, so they correctly return false.

