Approach: split each cell into 4 triangles (0=top, 1=right, 2=bottom, 3=left) and merge them with union-find.

- Within a cell, a blank space unites all four triangles.
- `/` unites top with left (0 and 3) and right with bottom (1 and 2).
- `\` unites top with right (0 and 1) and bottom with left (2 and 3).
- Across cells, the bottom triangle (2) of cell (i,j) unites with the top triangle (0) of cell (i+1,j). The right triangle (1) of cell (i,j) unites with the left triangle (3) of cell (i,j+1).

The answer is the number of distinct components. The cell index is `i*n+j` and the triangle id is `4*(i*n+j)+k`.

```java
class Solution {
    int[] p;
    int find(int x) {
        while (p[x] != x) {
            p[x] = p[p[x]];
            x = p[x];
        }
        return x;
    }
    void union(int a, int b) {
        int ra = find(a), rb = find(b);
        if (ra != rb) p[ra] = rb;
    }
    public int regionsBySlashes(String[] grid) {
        int n = grid.length;
        p = new int[4 * n * n];
        for (int i = 0; i < p.length; i++) p[i] = i;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                int b = 4 * (i * n + j);
                char c = grid[i].charAt(j);
                if (c == ' ') {
                    union(b, b + 1);
                    union(b, b + 2);
                    union(b, b + 3);
                } else if (c == '/') {
                    union(b, b + 3);
                    union(b + 1, b + 2);
                } else {
                    union(b, b + 1);
                    union(b + 2, b + 3);
                }
                if (i + 1 < n) {
                    union(b + 2, 4 * ((i + 1) * n + j));
                }
                if (j + 1 < n) {
                    union(b + 1, 4 * (i * n + j + 1) + 3);
                }
            }
        }
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
            if (find(i) == i) count++;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

