Build an adjacency map from the pairs. The two endpoints of `nums` are the only values that appear in exactly one pair, so any value with a single neighbor can be the start. From there, walk the chain: each next element is the neighbor that isn't the previous one.

Each value has at most 2 neighbors, so I store them in a `HashMap<Integer, int[]>` with a count array, or in a `HashMap<Integer, List<Integer>>`. To keep it fast, I use an offset of 100000 and arrays of size 200001: `a[v][0]` and `a[v][1]` hold the neighbors, initialized to a sentinel, and `cnt[v]` is the degree.

Steps:
1. For each pair (u, v), add v to u's neighbor slots and u to v's.
2. Find a value with degree 1 and use it as the start.
3. Set `res[0] = start` and `res[1] = its only neighbor`.
4. For i ≥ 2, `res[i]` is the neighbor of `res[i-1]` that differs from `res[i-2]`. Values are unique, so this is unambiguous.

Since n = pairs.length + 1, the answer has that length. For the start search, I iterate over the pairs and check `cnt` for each endpoint.

```java
class Solution {
    public int[] restoreArray(int[][] adjacentPairs) {
        int OFF = 100000;
        int[][] a = new int[200001][2];
        int[] cnt = new int[200001];
        for (int[] p : adjacentPairs) {
            int u = p[0] + OFF, v = p[1] + OFF;
            a[u][cnt[u]++] = v;
            a[v][cnt[v]++] = u;
        }
        int n = adjacentPairs.length + 1;
        int start = -1;
        for (int[] p : adjacentPairs) {
            int u = p[0] + OFF, v = p[1] + OFF;
            if (cnt[u] == 1) {
                start = u;
                break;
            }
            if (cnt[v] == 1) {
                start = v;
                break;
            }
        }
        int[] res = new int[n];
        res[0] = start - OFF;
        int prev = -1, cur = start;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            int next;
            if (a[cur][0] != prev && cnt[cur] >= 1) {
                next = a[cur][0];
            } else {
                next = a[cur][1];
            }
            res[i] = next - OFF;
            prev = cur;
            cur = next;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

