Track the robot's horizontal and vertical offsets while scanning the string. `R` adds 1 to x, `L` subtracts 1, `U` adds 1 to y, and `D` subtracts 1. The robot is back at the origin exactly when both offsets are 0.

The examples show a trailing space in the input (`"UD "`). Any character other than the four valid moves is ignored, so the space has no effect.

