Scan the key presses once, tracking the longest duration seen so far and the key that achieved it. For each press, compute its duration as `releaseTimes[i] - releaseTimes[i-1]` (or `releaseTimes[0]` for the first press). If the duration is longer than the best, take this key. If it ties the best, keep whichever key is lexicographically larger.

```java
class Solution {
    public char slowestKey(int[] releaseTimes, String keysPressed) {
        int best = releaseTimes[0];
        char key = keysPressed.charAt(0);
        for (int i = 1; i < releaseTimes.length; i++) {
            int d = releaseTimes[i] - releaseTimes[i - 1];
            char c = keysPressed.charAt(i);
            if (d > best || (d == best && c > key)) {
                best = d;
                key = c;
            }
        }
        return key;
    }
}
```

