Encode each number as a single sort key, `bitCount * 100000 + value`. Values are at most 10^4, so the value part never overflows into the bit-count part. Sorting the encoded keys orders by bit count first and by value second. Then decode each key with `% 100000`.

```java
class Solution {
    public int[] sortByBits(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        int[] keys = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            keys[i] = Integer.bitCount(arr[i]) * 100000 + arr[i];
        }
        java.util.Arrays.sort(keys);
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            arr[i] = keys[i] % 100000;
        }
        return arr;
    }
}
```

