inference_trace:
A word is uncommon exactly when it appears once in the combined text of both sentences. So I count every word across `s1` and `s2` and keep the words whose total count is 1.

```java
import java.util.*;

class Solution {
    public String[] uncommonFromSentences(String s1, String s2) {
        Map<String, Integer> count = new LinkedHashMap<>();
        for (String w : (s1 + " " + s2).split(" ")) {
            count.merge(w, 1, Integer::sum);
        }
        List<String> res = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> e : count.entrySet()) {
            if (e.getValue() == 1) res.add(e.getKey());
        }
        return res.toArray(new String[0]);
    }
}
```

